(c) whether Government has any data on the number of cases pending in these Courts and if so, the details thereof?

(a) the steps being taken by Government to ensure universal access to quality education, particularly in rural and underserved areas of the country specifically in the State of Punjab;
(b) whether Government has any mechanism to ensure that education is accessible to children with disabilities and the manner in which schools are being made more inclusive;
(c) the manner in which Government is addressing the challenges of illiteracy in certain areas, especially in tribal and marginalized communities; and
(d) the measures being taken by Government to bridge the gap in educational access between urban and rural areas?

(a) whether Government has formulated or proposes to formulate a policy for providing free annual preventive health check-ups and diagnostic tests to every citizen for early detection of communicable and non-communicable diseases;
(b) if so, the details thereof, including the proposed age groups, categories of beneficiaries, package of diagnostic tests, implementation mechanism and likely timeline; and
(c) if not, whether Government has examined the feasibility of introducing such a nationwide preventive health screening programme, and the reasons therefor?

(a) national monitoring systems or digital platforms that are currently used to track water quality, groundwater pollution and river health across the country;
(b) whether there are any long-term national plans or targets for ensuring safe drinking water and pollution-free rivers by a specific year, if so, the details thereof; and
(c) steps being taken to ensure public transparency and citizen participation in monitoring water pollution and protecting water resources?

(a) whether Government is considering policy measures to maintain reasonable airfare levels to promote wider accessibility of air travel for the general public specially in the State of Punjab;
(b) the role of schemes such as UDAN (Ude Desh ka Aam Nagrik) in ensuring affordable regional air connectivity; and
(c) whether Government proposes to expand affordable air travel options and regulate fare spikes on high-demand domestic and international routes?

(a) whether complaints have been received regarding corruption, bribery or exploitation of citizens at various passport offices, such as Regional Passport Offices or Passport Seva Kendras during the last five years;
(b) if so, the details thereof, including the name of the passport office, city and the number of complaints; and
(c) the details of investigations conducted and the number of cases in which action has been taken?

(a) whether Government publishes any official report that provides data on the percentage of land under forest cover for India and for individual States;
