(c) whether the income growth achieved in Punjab is in line with the original targets and revised benchmarks and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the main barriers that prevent the full implementation of environmental protection laws and cleanliness regulations in the country;
(b) whether there is any system in place to audit or review the effectiveness of these laws and ensure timely implementation at both the Central and State levels; and
(c) the role of local Governments (urban bodies, panchayats) in enforcing environmental laws and the manner in which their performance is monitored?

(a) how many National Highway–related projects are currently underway in the State of Punjab, the district-wise and project-wise status and by when will they be completed;
(b) how many projects are under consideration and the expected timeline for their approval and commencement;
(c) how many projects are stalled, how long they have been stalled (project-wise) and the reasons for stalling of projects;
(d) whether any penalties have been imposed on contractors or concessionaires for delays; and
(e) what action is proposed or taken by the Ministry if these projects are not completed within the revised timelines?

(a) considering that a significant number of deaths in the country are attributed to unknown causes or undiagnosed diseases, whether Government have any policy under which all citizens, especially those from economically weaker sections, can avail of free annual full-body health checkups;
(b) if such a scheme exists, the details thereof and how a common person can avail the service through Government hospitals or health camps; and
(c) if no such scheme exists yet, whether the Ministry is working on launching any preventive health screening program at the national level to help detect life-threatening diseases early and reduce mortality?

(a) whether Government maintains record of the total debt waived off or written off in respect of corporates and farmers from April 2014 to the current financial year, if so, the details thereof;
(b) the State/UT-wise and sector-wise details of such debt waivers/write-offs separately for corporates and farmers; and
(c) whether Government has undertaken any comparative assessment of the impact of corporate debt write-offs vis-à-vis farmers’ debt relief on public finances and economic equity?

(a) whether Government proposes to start direct domestic flights from Amritsar, Adampur and Mohali airports in the State of Punjab to Takht Sri Patna Sahib and Takht Sri Hazur Sahib, keeping in view the religious importance of these destinations;
(b) if so, the details of the proposal along with the expected timeline for commencement of such flights; and
