(a) whether IndiGo or any other airline has compensated passengers stranded at airports due to flight cancellations and delays;
(b) if so, the details of compensation paid and the guidelines followed; and
(c) the action taken by Government against airlines for charging exorbitant air fares during crisis situations, including regulatory or punitive measures imposed?

(a) what initiatives are being undertaken to educate the public about the importance of pollution control and the impact of environmental degradation on health and livelihoods;
(b) whether there are any specific programmes targeting schools, colleges and communities to raise awareness about waste management, air pollution and water conservation; and
(c) the details of Government plans to use technology and media to encourage responsible environmental behaviour among citizens, particularly in high-risk pollution areas?

(a) whether Government has identified agents, intermediaries or international trafficking networks involved in cheating Indian youth by offering fake jobs and illegally sending them to the Russian Army;
(b) the details of criminal, legal and diplomatic actions that have been initiated against such individuals or networks, both within India and abroad; and
(c) whether Government is engaging with Russian authorities to ensure accountability, justice and prevention of such incidents in future?

(a) specific steps being taken by Government to modernize agriculture and make farmers more economically empowered, especially in terms of technology, education, and access to modern farming techniques;
(b) whether there are any skill development programs, training sessions, or subsidies available to help farmers adopt advanced farming practices, improve yields, and access global markets; and
(c) the manner in which Government is encouraging the use of alternative income sources or non-farm-based activities to improve the economic condition of farmers?

(a) the details of stubble burning cases across various States, particularly in Punjab, from 2022 to 2025 along with the most affected districts;
(b) the steps being taken to curb stubble burning and the manner in which Government is coordinating with State Governments to mitigate this issue; and
(c) whether there are any successful models or alternative solutions in certain districts that could be replicated in other States to reduce stubble burning?

(a) whether a significant number of young people from India seek higher education abroad and whether Government has conducted any study to understand the causes and trends of this migration, if so, the details thereof;
(b) in light of the increasing number of students going abroad for education, whether Government is exploring any initiatives to encourage students to pursue higher education within the country instead; and
(c) whether there are any policies or programs in place that aim to retain talented students and offer them high-quality education and employment opportunities within India, thereby preventing the outflow of talent and resources?

(a) whether Government has a formal policy or programme to identify, reward and promote Panchayats that have implemented innovative development models or achieved outstanding results in rural development;
(b) the efforts in place to replicate the successful initiatives of such model Panchayats across other villages, including documentation, exposure visits or best-practice sharing platforms; and
(c) whether the Ministry has considered creating a national database of high-performing Panchayats so that their achievements and methodologies can be widely shared and adopted by others?

(a) the schemes or awareness campaigns launched to educate farmers on the balanced use of fertilizers, including organic and bio-fertilizers;
(b) the manner in which Government is ensuring last-mile delivery and availability of fertilizers in remote and rural areas; and
(c) whether there are any incentives or subsidy programs being provided to encourage the use of micronutrients and customized fertilizers?

(a) whether Government has established any national policy, project or time-bound programme for regular de-silting of rivers, rivulets, drains and streams in flood-prone States, especially State of Punjab, if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether any central funding mechanism exists for de-silting of rivers and drainage channels under Flood Management Programme, River Rejuvenation Projects or catchment area improvement initiatives, if so, the amount sanctioned, if not, the reasons therefor; and
(c) if not, specific project or timeline that has been set for de-silting, the reasons for delay in its formulation and whether Government plans to introduce a dedicated national desiltation mission to prevent future flooding in northern States?

(a) total number of dams existing in the country along with the year of construction of each dam and the State-wise name of these dams;
(b) whether these dams have undergone de-silting or desiltation operations since their construction; if so, the details and timeline of such work, and if not, the reasons for non-implementation of de-silting despite repeated silt accumulation concerns; and
(c) whether Government is maintaining updated technical data on the current storage capacity of all dams and whether any studies conducted to examine the loss of live storage due to siltation, if so, the findings, and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) despite the country's overall development, farmers do not receive their rightful Minimum Support Price (MSP) for their crops, the underlying reasons for the same;
